# task 08 average — expected output: 0.498046875
# build: unicon -s 08_average.icn    run: 08_average.exe
# Unicon's `real` is a C double. Every reading is an exact multiple of 1/256 and the total
# stays under 2^53, so the sum is exact and the printed digits do not depend on the order of
# addition. `write` prints a real with enough digits to round-trip here.

procedure main()
    total := 0.0
    every i := 0 to 99999999 do
        total +:= (i % 256) / 256.0
    write(total / 100000000)
end
